{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"401ac5e1","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008611,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:35.853658+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:35.845047+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# PS26162 — CatBoost Proper Final Training Notebook — Source-fixed, rerun required\n","\n","This notebook contains the source-level fixes for the final 2-year CatBoost training workflow. Saved execution outputs are intentionally cleared; a fresh top-to-bottom run is required before any metric is treated as evidence.\n","\n","## Locked evaluation design\n","\n","TRAIN:\n","- Maharashtra\n","- Karnataka\n","- Madhya Pradesh\n","- Punjab\n","- Andhra Pradesh\n","- Telangana\n","\n","TEST A:\n","- Gujarat\n","- Tamil Nadu\n","\n","TEST B:\n","- Jharkhand\n","- Rajasthan\n","\n","### Important methodological rules\n","\n","1. The support gate is applied to the **combined geographic partitions**, matching the executed OSI/WRI support check. It is NOT applied separately to every state.\n","2. Test A and Test B are not used for Optuna tuning, early stopping, feature selection, threshold selection, or tree-count selection.\n","3. Internal validation is created only from TRAIN states.\n","4. Internal validation uses deterministic H3-parent blocking and is selected **without looking at labels**.\n","5. `h3_lat` and `h3_lon` are excluded from model inputs.\n","6. `state`, `label`, `is_labeled`, and `acq_date` are excluded from model inputs.\n","7. `h3_08` and `daynight` are handled as native CatBoost categorical features.\n","8. `auto_class_weights=\"Balanced\"` is retained.\n","9. Current `satellite_nunique` is retained. No missing satellite identity is fabricated.\n","10. The current Phase 6 labels are bootstrap/pseudo-labels. Therefore model metrics describe generalization of the labeling scheme, not independent ground-truth accuracy.\n","\n","## Blind-test policy\n","\n","The notebook does not calculate Test A/Test B support or class distributions before model selection. The previously completed OSI/WRI support audit is treated as the frozen partition-integrity artifact.\n","\n","The blind labels are only consumed when the final model is evaluated at the end of the notebook.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"2755b114","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T17:37:35.869659Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T17:37:35.868986Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.633917Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.633157Z"},"papermill":{"duration":4.774755,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.635612+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:35.860857+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m1.1/1.1 MB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m46.4 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\r\n","\u001b[?25h"]}],"source":["!pip install -q catboost optuna \"h3>=4.0,<5\"\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"631af0c8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.652465Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.652121Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.361349Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.360414Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.719912,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.362982+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:40.64307+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Runtime versions: {\"catboost\": \"1.2.10\", \"h3\": \"4.5.0\", \"numpy\": \"2.0.2\", \"optuna\": \"4.9.0\", \"pandas\": \"2.3.3\", \"python\": \"3.12.13\"}\n","Configuration loaded.\n"]}],"source":["import hashlib\n","import json\n","import platform\n","import warnings\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","from sklearn.metrics import (\n","    classification_report,\n","    confusion_matrix,\n","    f1_score,\n",")\n","\n","import catboost\n","from catboost import CatBoostClassifier, Pool\n","import optuna\n","import h3\n","\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n","\n","PACKAGE_VERSIONS = {\n","    \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n","    \"catboost\": catboost.__version__,\n","    \"optuna\": optuna.__version__,\n","    \"h3\": h3.__version__,\n","    \"pandas\": pd.__version__,\n","    \"numpy\": np.__version__,\n","}\n","print(\"Runtime versions:\", json.dumps(PACKAGE_VERSIONS, sort_keys=True))\n","\n","RANDOM_SEED = 42\n","\n","TARGET = \"label\"\n","LABEL_FLAG = \"is_labeled\"\n","STATE_COL = \"state\"\n","ID_COL = \"h3_08\"\n","\n","TRAIN_STATES = [\n","    \"Maharashtra\",\n","    \"Karnataka\",\n","    \"Madhya Pradesh\",\n","    \"Punjab\",\n","    \"Andhra Pradesh\",\n","    \"Telangana\",\n","]\n","\n","TEST_A_STATES = [\"Gujarat\", \"Tamil Nadu\"]\n","TEST_B_STATES = [\"Jharkhand\", \"Rajasthan\"]\n","\n","# Every state this training run is allowed to see, in any role. Spec 4.1\n","# requires filtering to exactly this partition before any split -- the\n","# labeling notebook confirmed rows exist outside it (West Bengal, Odisha,\n","# Chhattisgarh, etc.) and they must not silently ride along in any\n","# dataset-level statistic (e.g. cell 7's feature-missingness table).\n","LOCKED_STATES = TRAIN_STATES + TEST_A_STATES + TEST_B_STATES\n","\n","CLASSES = [\n","    \"industrial\",\n","    \"mining\",\n","    \"agricultural_burn\",\n","    \"wildfire\",\n","]\n","\n","DATA_FILENAME = \"sih2026_h3_daily_labeled.parquet\"\n","# Set this only when multiple files with DATA_FILENAME are attached. Otherwise\n","# the notebook refuses ambiguity instead of silently selecting a stale artifact.\n","DATA_PATH = None\n","DATE_COL = \"acq_date\"\n","\n","# Verified fact from the rebuild prompt: a real, error-free execution of the\n","# fixed osi-wri-data.ipynb produced a labeled parquet of exactly this shape.\n","# Checked in cell 3 before anything else happens.\n","EXPECTED_DATASET_SHAPE = (1442545, 61)  # UPDATED: 58 + 3 (acq_month, doy_sin, doy_cos added by data-eda.ipynb Phase 8C)\n","\n","EXCLUDE_COLS = {\n","    TARGET,\n","    LABEL_FLAG,\n","    STATE_COL,\n","    \"acq_date\",\n","    \"h3_lat\",\n","    \"h3_lon\",\n","    # Source-derived and state-join provenance fields must never be model inputs.\n","    \"is_static_land\",\n","    \"is_offshore\",\n","    \"state_assignment_method\",\n","    \"_state_distance_km\",\n","}\n","\n","CAT_FEATURES_REQUESTED = [\"h3_08\", \"daynight\"]\n","\n","# These fields directly participate in the Phase 6 rule cascade. They remain\n","# in the locked baseline to measure geographic generalization of that cascade,\n","# never as evidence of independent ground-truth accuracy.\n","RULE_DIRECT_FEATURES = {\n","    \"frp_max\",\n","    \"is_first_observation\",\n","    \"active_days_90d\",\n","    \"is_saturated_max\",\n","    \"dist_osm_industrial_km\",\n","    \"dist_osm_quarry_km\",\n","    \"dist_osm_mineshaft_km\",\n","    \"dist_osm_adit_km\",\n","    \"dist_osm_farmland_km\",\n","    \"dist_osm_power_infra_km\",\n","    \"dist_wri_gas_km\",\n","    \"dist_wri_oil_km\",\n","}\n","\n","# These are the frozen partition-support results from the completed\n","# OSI/WRI audit. They are documentation/integrity references only and\n","# are NOT used to choose anything in this training notebook -- they are\n","# used to VERIFY that the attached dataset is the correct, fixed one\n","# (see cell 5 and cell 23), not to select anything.\n","#\n","# CORRECTED 2026-09-04 (supersedes and explains the 2026-09-01 entry below).\n","#\n","# What happened: the 2026-09-01 edit found that the reference values\n","# (train=386, test_a=46, test_b=341) did not match the dataset attached at\n","# that time, and RESOLVED the mismatch by overwriting FROZEN_SUPPORT to match\n","# the attached data (train=9974, test_a=757, test_b=1794) instead of stopping\n","# to diagnose. That was the wrong call. Root cause, now confirmed: the\n","# attached parquet (dataset_sha256 781f2c5911d5c4b5c61236f58909361abfbf09b5c34\n","# bcdb90662a9541377cb3) was built with the OLD, buggy\n","# mining_persistence_days=1 (an argmax(gap) bug, mathematically forced to\n","# day 1 on a convex decreasing curve -- a near no-op filter). That inflates\n","# mining support ~25x. It is not a real change in the underlying data.\n","#\n","# The correct, LOCKED values below come from a real, error-free execution\n","# of the FIXED labeling notebook (osi-wri-data.ipynb, mining_persistence_days\n","# hardcoded to 5 after the day-4/day-5 statistical tie was found and\n","# disclosed; sequential exec_count 1->24, zero errors). These are the values\n","# this training notebook must see. If cell 5 or cell 23 raise a mismatch\n","# against these numbers, DO NOT edit this dict to match -- it means the\n","# wrong parquet is attached. Stop and re-check the dataset source/version.\n","#\n","# NOTE: only the mining count has a verified locked reference for TRAIN.\n","# Industrial/agricultural_burn/wildfire TRAIN counts are not independently\n","# pinned here because no verified number for them exists in the source\n","# document -- do not fabricate one. Cell 5 still floors all four classes at\n","# MIN_TRAIN_CELLS; only mining gets the exact-match identity check.\n","FROZEN_SUPPORT = {\n","    \"train_mining_h3_cells\": 388,\n","    \"test_a_mining_h3_cells\": 47,\n","    \"test_b_mining_h3_cells\": 342,\n","}\n","\n","# Optional hard dataset-identity gate. Once you've confirmed a run against\n","# the correct parquet, paste its dataset_sha256 (printed in cell 3) here to\n","# make future stale-data errors impossible to miss, not just plausible to\n","# miss. Leave as None until you have that confirmed hash -- a None value\n","# only triggers a WARNING in cell 3, not a hard failure.\n","EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256 = None\n","\n","MIN_TRAIN_CELLS = 100\n","# Applied to TEST A/B support for every class in cell 23 (not just mining) --\n","# previously defined but never actually checked anywhere.\n","MIN_TEST_CELLS = 30\n","\n","OUT = Path(\"/kaggle/working/PS26162_catboost_final\")\n","OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","print(\"Configuration loaded.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"ab987ac7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.379502Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.3791Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.349774Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.348932Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.980598,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.351422+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:44.370824+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Using: /kaggle/input/datasets/dptel22/osi-parquet/sih2026_h3_daily_labeled.parquet\n","Dataset SHA-256: fbdd86cbc0e396cd8e057894f592ef56e5ed2d5db05396ce440bafc813f39333\n","Shape: (1442545, 61)\n","WARNING: EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256 is not set in cell 2 -- this run cannot verify it is using the intended dataset version by hash alone. The live partition-support checks in cell 5 and cell 23 are the actual safety net until you set this.\n","Dropping 636,106 rows outside the locked 10-state partition (states present: ['Andaman & Nicobar', 'Arunachal Pradesh', 'Assam', 'Bihar', 'Chandigarh', 'Chhattisgarh', 'Daman and Diu and Dadra and Nagar Haveli', 'Delhi', 'Goa', 'Haryana', 'Himachal Pradesh', 'Jammu and Kashmir', 'Kerala', 'Ladakh', 'Manipur', 'Meghalaya', 'Mizoram', 'Nagaland', 'Odisha', 'Puducherry', 'Sikkim', 'Tripura', 'Uttar Pradesh', 'Uttarakhand', 'West Bengal']).\n","Shape after locked-partition filter: (806439, 61)\n","Total rows: 806,439\n","Labeled rows: 405,214\n","Unlabeled rows: 401,225\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>rows</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>label</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>industrial</th>\n","      <td>282859</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>mining</th>\n","      <td>68097</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>agricultural_burn</th>\n","      <td>8968</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>wildfire</th>\n","      <td>45290</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                     rows\n","label                    \n","industrial         282859\n","mining              68097\n","agricultural_burn    8968\n","wildfire            45290"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["def find_data_file(filename):\n","    if DATA_PATH is not None:\n","        path = Path(DATA_PATH)\n","        if not path.is_file():\n","            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Configured DATA_PATH does not exist: {path}\")\n","        return path\n","\n","    roots = [Path(\"/kaggle/input\"), Path(\"/kaggle/working\")]\n","    matches = sorted(\n","        {\n","            path.resolve()\n","            for root in roots if root.exists()\n","            for path in root.rglob(filename)\n","        }\n","    )\n","    if len(matches) == 1:\n","        return matches[0]\n","    if not matches:\n","        raise FileNotFoundError(\n","            f\"Could not find {filename}. Attach the labeled Phase 6 dataset.\"\n","        )\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Multiple labeled parquet candidates found. Set DATA_PATH explicitly: \"\n","        f\"{[str(path) for path in matches]}\"\n","    )\n","\n","def sha256_file(path, chunk_size=1024 * 1024):\n","    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n","    with open(path, \"rb\") as handle:\n","        for chunk in iter(lambda: handle.read(chunk_size), b\"\"):\n","            digest.update(chunk)\n","    return digest.hexdigest()\n","\n","\n","data_path = find_data_file(DATA_FILENAME)\n","df = pd.read_parquet(data_path)\n","\n","# Hard shape gate. Spec 4.1: stop immediately on a wrong artifact, before any\n","# downstream parsing, hashing, filtering, feature audit, or splitting.\n","assert df.shape == EXPECTED_DATASET_SHAPE, (\n","    f\"Dataset shape mismatch. Expected {EXPECTED_DATASET_SHAPE}, got {df.shape}. \"\n","    \"Wrong file attached -- stop before doing anything else.\"\n",")\n","# This flag records that the RAW, pre-filter shape was checked and passed.\n","# BUG FIX (this pass): the final run_integrity object was comparing\n","# df.shape against EXPECTED_DATASET_SHAPE again at the very end of the\n","# notebook -- but by then df has been correctly, deliberately filtered\n","# down to the locked 10-state partition a few lines below this cell, so\n","# df.shape never equals the raw pre-filter shape again for the rest of the\n","# run. That re-check compared a post-filter variable to a pre-filter\n","# constant and could never pass on any run -- it cost a full ~5.8hr run.\n","# Fix: capture \"the raw shape check passed\" once, here, before filtering,\n","# and have the final audit reference this flag instead of recomputing a\n","# stale comparison against a variable that legitimately changes shape.\n","dataset_shape_gate_passed = True\n","\n","dataset_sha256 = sha256_file(data_path)\n","df[DATE_COL] = pd.to_datetime(df[DATE_COL], errors=\"raise\")\n","\n","print(\"Using:\", data_path)\n","print(\"Dataset SHA-256:\", dataset_sha256)\n","print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n","\n","if EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256 is None:\n","    print(\n","        \"WARNING: EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256 is not set in cell 2 -- this run \"\n","        \"cannot verify it is using the intended dataset version by hash \"\n","        \"alone. The live partition-support checks in cell 5 and cell 23 \"\n","        \"are the actual safety net until you set this.\"\n","    )\n","elif dataset_sha256 != EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Dataset SHA-256 does not match EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256. \"\n","        f\"Expected {EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256}, got {dataset_sha256}. \"\n","        \"Wrong dataset version attached -- stop, do not proceed.\"\n","    )\n","else:\n","    print(\"Dataset SHA-256 matches EXPECTED_DATASET_SHA256. Confirmed correct version.\")\n","\n","# Mandatory partition filter (spec 4.1). Previously entirely absent -- the\n","# labeling notebook confirmed rows exist outside the locked 10-state\n","# partition (e.g. mining rows in West Bengal/Odisha/Chhattisgarh) and the\n","# saved parquet does not filter them out. Every downstream split already\n","# happens to scope itself via .isin(TRAIN/TEST_A/TEST_B_STATES), so this\n","# was not silently leaking into training -- but dataset-level statistics\n","# (e.g. cell 7's feature-missingness table) were being computed over the\n","# full, unfiltered, all-India data without disclosure. Fixed here.\n","_stray_mask = ~df[STATE_COL].isin(LOCKED_STATES)\n","_n_stray = int(_stray_mask.sum())\n","if _n_stray:\n","    _stray_states = sorted(df.loc[_stray_mask, STATE_COL].dropna().unique())\n","    print(\n","        f\"Dropping {_n_stray:,} rows outside the locked 10-state partition \"\n","        f\"(states present: {_stray_states}).\"\n","    )\n","else:\n","    print(\"No rows found outside the locked 10-state partition.\")\n","df = df.loc[~_stray_mask].copy()\n","print(\"Shape after locked-partition filter:\", df.shape)\n","\n","required = {TARGET, LABEL_FLAG, STATE_COL, ID_COL, \"daynight\"}\n","missing = sorted(required - set(df.columns))\n","if missing:\n","    raise ValueError(f\"Missing required columns: {missing}\")\n","\n","if df.empty:\n","    raise ValueError(\"Dataset is empty.\")\n","\n","if not df[LABEL_FLAG].isin([0, 1]).all():\n","    raise ValueError(f\"{LABEL_FLAG} must contain only 0/1 values.\")\n","if df.loc[df[LABEL_FLAG] == 1, TARGET].isna().any():\n","    raise ValueError(\"A labeled row has a missing target.\")\n","if df.loc[df[LABEL_FLAG] == 0, TARGET].notna().any():\n","    raise ValueError(\"An unlabeled row has a target; fix the Phase 6 artifact.\")\n","\n","labeled = df[df[LABEL_FLAG] == 1].copy()\n","labeled[TARGET] = labeled[TARGET].astype(str)\n","\n","observed_classes = sorted(labeled[TARGET].unique())\n","if observed_classes != sorted(CLASSES):\n","    raise ValueError(\n","        f\"Unexpected target classes. Expected {sorted(CLASSES)}, observed {observed_classes}\"\n","    )\n","\n","if labeled[ID_COL].isna().any():\n","    raise ValueError(\"Labeled rows contain missing h3_08 values.\")\n","\n","# The canonical H3-day product should have at most one row per H3 cell/date.\n","if DATE_COL in labeled.columns:\n","    duplicate_h3_days = labeled.duplicated([ID_COL, DATE_COL]).sum()\n","    if duplicate_h3_days:\n","        raise ValueError(\n","            f\"Found {duplicate_h3_days:,} duplicate labeled H3-day rows \"\n","            \"for (h3_08, acq_date). Fix the upstream aggregation before training.\"\n","        )\n","\n","# Catch impossible target availability states explicitly.\n","if labeled[TARGET].isna().any():\n","    raise ValueError(\"Some rows are marked labeled but have a missing target.\")\n","\n","print(\"Total rows:\", f\"{len(df):,}\")\n","print(\"Labeled rows:\", f\"{len(labeled):,}\")\n","print(\"Unlabeled rows:\", f\"{len(df) - len(labeled):,}\")\n","\n","class_counts = (\n","    labeled[TARGET]\n","    .value_counts()\n","    .reindex(CLASSES, fill_value=0)\n",")\n","\n","display(class_counts.to_frame(\"rows\"))\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"26fa0603","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.368617Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.368201Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.245323Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.244436Z"},"papermill":{"duration":96.895282,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.254997+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:37:48.359715+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Temporal leakage audit: PASS (shift-before-rolling reproduced exactly, both frp and active-day lags now checked against the same excludes-today convention).\n"]}],"source":["# Adversarial temporal-feature audit. This recomputes the available\n","# historical features from the parquet without reading labels or changing the\n","# model matrix. It verifies the upstream shift-before-rolling contract before\n","# any spatial split or hyperparameter tuning occurs.\n","#\n","# SELF-CORRECTION (logged, not silent): the previous version of this cell\n","# built `_active_prev` from `groupby(ID_COL).cumcount().gt(0)` and rolled it\n","# WITHOUT shifting, while `_frp_prev` was correctly shifted by 1 before\n","# rolling. That asymmetry meant the active-days reconstruction included the\n","# current day's own detection in its trailing-window count, while the FRP\n","# reconstruction correctly excluded it -- i.e. the two lag features were\n","# being audited against two different leakage conventions. Fixed below by\n","# shifting a per-row \"this is a detection day\" indicator by 1, exactly\n","# mirroring the FRP treatment, so both audits check the same \"excludes\n","# today\" contract.\n","TEMPORAL_AUDIT_COLUMNS = {\n","    \"frp_max_lag7\",\n","    \"frp_max_lag30\",\n","    \"active_days_7d\",\n","    \"active_days_30d\",\n","    \"active_days_90d\",\n","}\n","missing_temporal = sorted(TEMPORAL_AUDIT_COLUMNS - set(df.columns))\n","if missing_temporal:\n","    raise ValueError(f\"Missing temporal features: {missing_temporal}\")\n","\n","_temporal = df[[ID_COL, DATE_COL, \"frp_max\"]].copy()\n","if _temporal.duplicated([ID_COL, DATE_COL]).any():\n","    raise ValueError(\"Cannot audit temporal features: duplicate H3-day rows found.\")\n","_temporal = _temporal.sort_values([ID_COL, DATE_COL]).reset_index(drop=True)\n","_temporal[\"_frp_prev\"] = _temporal.groupby(ID_COL, sort=False)[\"frp_max\"].shift(1)\n","\n","# Every row is, by construction, a detection day. Shift that indicator by 1\n","# (grouped) so the rolling window sums PRIOR detection days only, matching\n","# _frp_prev's leakage-safe convention exactly.\n","_temporal[\"_is_detection_day\"] = 1\n","_temporal[\"_active_prev\"] = (\n","    _temporal.groupby(ID_COL, sort=False)[\"_is_detection_day\"]\n","    .shift(1)\n","    .fillna(0)\n","    .astype(\"int8\")\n",")\n","\n","\n","def expected_history(window):\n","    rolled = (\n","        _temporal\n","        .groupby(ID_COL, sort=False)\n","        .rolling(window, on=DATE_COL, min_periods=1)[[\"_frp_prev\", \"_active_prev\"]]\n","        .agg({\"_frp_prev\": \"max\", \"_active_prev\": \"sum\"})\n","        .reset_index()\n","    )\n","    if not rolled[[ID_COL, DATE_COL]].reset_index(drop=True).equals(\n","        _temporal[[ID_COL, DATE_COL]].reset_index(drop=True)\n","    ):\n","        raise AssertionError(f\"{window} historical rolling output is misaligned.\")\n","    return rolled\n","\n","_expected_7 = expected_history(\"7D\")\n","_expected_30 = expected_history(\"30D\")\n","_expected_90 = expected_history(\"90D\")\n","\n","for actual_name, expected_values in {\n","    \"frp_max_lag7\": _expected_7[\"_frp_prev\"],\n","    \"frp_max_lag30\": _expected_30[\"_frp_prev\"],\n","    \"active_days_7d\": _expected_7[\"_active_prev\"],\n","    \"active_days_30d\": _expected_30[\"_active_prev\"],\n","    \"active_days_90d\": _expected_90[\"_active_prev\"],\n","}.items():\n","    actual = (\n","        df[[ID_COL, DATE_COL, actual_name]]\n","        .sort_values([ID_COL, DATE_COL])[actual_name]\n","        .to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","    )\n","    expected = expected_values.to_numpy(dtype=float)\n","    np.testing.assert_allclose(actual, expected, equal_nan=True)\n","\n","_first_rows = _temporal.groupby(ID_COL, sort=False).cumcount().eq(0)\n","assert _temporal.loc[_first_rows, \"_frp_prev\"].isna().all()\n","assert _temporal.loc[_first_rows, \"_active_prev\"].eq(0).all()\n","\n","del _expected_7, _expected_30, _expected_90, _temporal\n","print(\"Temporal leakage audit: PASS (shift-before-rolling reproduced exactly, \"\n","      \"both frp and active-day lags now checked against the same excludes-today convention).\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"a9252e37","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.271422Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.27101Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.397476Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.396444Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.136441,"end_time":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.398966+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T17:39:25.262525+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Current combined TRAIN support:\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>unique_H3_cells</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>label</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>industrial</th>\n","      <td>129932</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>mining</th>\n","      <td>388</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>agricultural_burn</th>\n","      <td>5289</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>wildfire</th>\n","      <td>37962</td>\n