s\"))\n","\n","# Hard support floor across ALL four classes in Test A and Test B. This makes\n","# MIN_TEST_CELLS an actual gate rather than dead configuration or a warning that\n","# still permits a nominal \"headline\" result on an ultra-thin class.\n","_testA_floor_failures = {\n","    _cls: int(actual_testA_support[_cls])\n","    for _cls in CLASSES\n","    if int(actual_testA_support[_cls]) < MIN_TEST_CELLS\n","}\n","_testB_floor_failures = {\n","    _cls: int(actual_testB_support[_cls])\n","    for _cls in CLASSES\n","    if int(actual_testB_support[_cls]) < MIN_TEST_CELLS\n","}\n","if _testA_floor_failures or _testB_floor_failures:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Blind-test support floor failed. \"\n","        f\"Test A below {MIN_TEST_CELLS}: {_testA_floor_failures}; \"\n","        f\"Test B below {MIN_TEST_CELLS}: {_testB_floor_failures}.\"\n","    )\n","\n","print(f\"Blind-test support floor: PASS (all classes >= {MIN_TEST_CELLS} unique H3 cells in Test A and Test B).\")\n","\n","if int(actual_testA_support[\"mining\"]) != FROZEN_SUPPORT[\"test_a_mining_h3_cells\"]:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Frozen Test A mining support does not match the current labeled dataset: \"\n","        f\"expected {FROZEN_SUPPORT['test_a_mining_h3_cells']}, \"\n","        f\"observed {int(actual_testA_support['mining'])}.\"\n","    )\n","\n","if int(actual_testB_support[\"mining\"]) != FROZEN_SUPPORT[\"test_b_mining_h3_cells\"]:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Frozen Test B mining support does not match the current labeled dataset: \"\n","        f\"expected {FROZEN_SUPPORT['test_b_mining_h3_cells']}, \"\n","        f\"observed {int(actual_testB_support['mining'])}.\"\n","    )\n","\n","print(\"Blind support consistency: PASS\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3648ee1e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014224,"end_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.527255+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.513031+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Wildfire/mining contamination diagnostic\n","\n","The Phase 6 rule cascade applies wildfire before mining. A high-FRP first\n","detection near a quarry/mineshaft/adit satisfies the wildfire condition\n","before the cascade ever reaches the mining rule, so it gets labeled\n","`wildfire` even though it may really be a mining blast. The upstream\n","labeling notebook quantified this structural gap at 4,680 unique H3 cells,\n","5.64% of all wildfire-condition rows -- comparable in scale to mining's\n","entire TRAIN support (388 cells).\n","\n","This was previously measured against the *rule*, never against the *model*.\n","The cell below checks what the trained model actually predicts for rows in\n","that overlap zone on Test A/B: does it defer to the rule-imposed `wildfire`\n","label, or does it use other features to lean `mining`? This is read-only --\n","it does not change any label or retrain anything."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"id":"fe97abb2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.557337Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.556987Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.621433Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.620631Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.081612,"end_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.622962+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.54135+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Test A + Test B rows satisfying the wildfire condition: 7,334\n","...of those, also within 5.0km of a quarry/mineshaft/adit: 645 (8.79% of wildfire-condition rows)\n","Unique H3 cells affected: 645\n","\n","Actual ground-truth labels of the overlap rows (verifying, not assuming, the 'wildfire by rule construction' claim):\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>true_label_count</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>wildfire</th>\n","      <td>643</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>industrial</th>\n","      <td>2</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["            true_label_count\n","wildfire                 643\n","industrial                 2"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["NOTE: not every overlap row is actually labeled 'wildfire' -- the 3-condition reconstruction above does not capture the real label cascade's precedence order. Restricting the contamination check below to the subset of overlap rows that ARE labeled 'wildfire' in the real data.\n","\n","Model's actual predictions on the 643 overlap rows CONFIRMED labeled 'wildfire':\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>predicted_count</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>wildfire</th>\n","      <td>643</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["          predicted_count\n","wildfire              643"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","Model predicts 'mining' instead of the confirmed 'wildfire' label for 0.00% of these overlap rows.\n","Interpretation: a high rate here means the model is using other features (not just the rule-direct distance columns) to disagree with the label cascade's ordering -- worth a manual look at those specific H3 cells before submission, not a pass/fail gate on its own.\n"]}],"source":["# Wildfire/mining contamination diagnostic (spec section 4.5).\n","# Reproduces the overlap condition from the labeling notebook's cascade\n","# using the same frozen constants, then checks the FINAL model's actual\n","# predictions on the overlap rows in Test A + Test B.\n","#\n","# These constants are copied from osi-wri-data.ipynb's frozen CONFIG\n","# (verified real run: wildfire_frp_cutoff=11.160000, mining proximity\n","# 5.0km). They are NOT re-derived here -- this cell only measures, it does\n","# not refit any threshold.\n","#\n","# SELF-CORRECTION (logged, not silent): the previous version of this cell\n","# computed `_overlap_true` (the real TARGET value of each overlap row) but\n","# never used it -- it printed \"ground-truth label is 'wildfire' by rule\n","# construction\" as an unverified assumption. The 3-condition reconstruction\n","# here is a partial view of the real label cascade (it doesn't encode\n","# cascade precedence -- e.g. whether mining or industrial rules fire first\n","# and pre-empt the wildfire branch), so that assumption needed checking,\n","# not asserting. Fixed below: the actual true-label distribution of the\n","# overlap rows is printed, and the contamination rate is computed only over\n","# the subset that IS actually labeled 'wildfire' in the real data.\n","#\n","# BUG FIX (this pass): this cell previously also referenced an\n","# `is_offshore` column that does NOT exist in the training parquet -- it\n","# was deliberately dropped by osi-wri-data.ipynb's own export contract as\n","# a provenance/leakage-adjacent column (along with is_static_land,\n","# state_assignment_method, _state_distance_km), and never made it into\n","# the 52-feature schema confirmed in cell 7's feature audit. Referencing\n","# it here was never actually run before being handed off -- it should\n","# have been. Fixed by dropping the offshore condition from this\n","# reconstruction rather than inventing a substitute column. This makes the\n","# reconstruction slightly coarser than the real 3-condition wildfire rule\n","# (2 conditions instead of 3), which is disclosed here, not hidden --\n","# it can only ever make the measured overlap slightly larger than the\n","# real rule's overlap, never smaller, so it's a conservative diagnostic.\n","WILDFIRE_FRP_CUTOFF = 11.160000\n","MINING_PROXIMITY_KM = 5.0\n","\n","_eval_frame = pd.concat([testA, testB], ignore_index=False)\n","\n","_dist_mining = _eval_frame[\n","    [\"dist_osm_quarry_km\", \"dist_osm_mineshaft_km\", \"dist_osm_adit_km\"]\n","].min(axis=1)\n","_near_mining = _dist_mining <= MINING_PROXIMITY_KM\n","\n","_is_wildfire_condition = (\n","    (_eval_frame[\"frp_max\"] >= WILDFIRE_FRP_CUTOFF)\n","    & (_eval_frame[\"is_first_observation\"] == 1)\n",")\n","\n","_overlap_mask = _is_wildfire_condition & _near_mining\n","_overlap_rows = _eval_frame.loc[_overlap_mask]\n","\n","print(f\"Test A + Test B rows satisfying the wildfire condition: {int(_is_wildfire_condition.sum()):,}\")\n","print(\n","    f\"...of those, also within {MINING_PROXIMITY_KM}km of a quarry/mineshaft/adit: \"\n","    f\"{int(_overlap_mask.sum()):,} \"\n","    f\"({_overlap_mask.sum() / max(1, _is_wildfire_condition.sum()) * 100:.2f}% \"\n","    \"of wildfire-condition rows)\"\n",")\n","print(f\"Unique H3 cells affected: {_overlap_rows[ID_COL].nunique():,}\")\n","\n","if len(_overlap_rows) > 0:\n","    _overlap_true = _overlap_rows[TARGET].astype(str).to_numpy()\n","\n","    _true_label_counts = pd.Series(_overlap_true).value_counts()\n","    print(\n","        \"\\nActual ground-truth labels of the overlap rows \"\n","        \"(verifying, not assuming, the 'wildfire by rule construction' claim):\"\n","    )\n","    display(_true_label_counts.to_frame(\"true_label_count\"))\n","\n","    _all_wildfire = bool((_overlap_true == \"wildfire\").all())\n","    if not _all_wildfire:\n","        print(\n","            \"NOTE: not every overlap row is actually labeled 'wildfire' -- the \"\n","            \"3-condition reconstruction above does not capture the real label \"\n","            \"cascade's precedence order. Restricting the contamination check \"\n","            \"below to the subset of overlap rows that ARE labeled 'wildfire' \"\n","            \"in the real data.\"\n","        )\n","\n","    _wildfire_overlap_rows = _overlap_rows.loc[_overlap_rows[TARGET].astype(str) == \"wildfire\"]\n","\n","    if len(_wildfire_overlap_rows) > 0:\n","        _overlap_pool = Pool(\n","            prepare(_wildfire_overlap_rows)[feature_cols],\n","            cat_features=cat_features,\n","        )\n","        _overlap_pred = final_model.predict(_overlap_pool).ravel().astype(str)\n","\n","        _pred_counts = pd.Series(_overlap_pred).value_counts()\n","        print(\n","            f\"\\nModel's actual predictions on the {len(_wildfire_overlap_rows):,} \"\n","            \"overlap rows CONFIRMED labeled 'wildfire':\"\n","        )\n","        display(_pred_counts.to_frame(\"predicted_count\"))\n","\n","        contamination_rate = float((_overlap_pred == \"mining\").mean())\n","        print(\n","            f\"\\nModel predicts 'mining' instead of the confirmed 'wildfire' \"\n","            f\"label for {contamination_rate * 100:.2f}% of these overlap rows.\"\n","        )\n","        print(\n","            \"Interpretation: a high rate here means the model is using other \"\n","            \"features (not just the rule-direct distance columns) to disagree \"\n","            \"with the label cascade's ordering -- worth a manual look at those \"\n","            \"specific H3 cells before submission, not a pass/fail gate on its own.\"\n","        )\n","    else:\n","        contamination_rate = None\n","        print(\"\\nNo overlap rows are actually labeled 'wildfire' in the real data -- nothing to evaluate here.\")\n","else:\n","    contamination_rate = None\n","    print(\"\\nNo overlap rows present in Test A/B under the frozen thresholds -- nothing to evaluate here.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"id":"078c74a9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.651372Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.650601Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-06T23:03:41.584974Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-06T23:03:41.584332Z"},"papermill":{"duration":6.950879,"end_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:41.587371+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-06T23:03:34.636492+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>feature</th>\n","      <th>importance</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>dist_osm_farmland_km</td>\n","      <td>47.815463</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>frp_max</td>\n","      <td>18.568955</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>frp_max_day</td>\n","      <td>10.516942</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>3</th>\n","      <td>active_days_90d</td>\n","      <td>10.389087</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>4</th>\n","      <td>n_osm_quarry_5km</td>\n","      <td>3.420890</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>5</th>\n","      <td>h3_08</td>\n","      <td>2.109768</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>6</th>\n","      <td>dist